after:
Here is the complete example.
```javascript
function textCounts(text) {
  let points = 0;
  for (const point of text) {
    points += 1;
  }
  return {units: text.length, points};
}
console.log(JSON.stringify(textCounts("A🌱")));
console.log(JSON.stringify(textCounts("e\u0301")));
```
Output:
```text
{"units":3,"points":2}
{"units":2,"points":2}
```
A and 🌱 make two code points, but need three storage units. In the second string, `\u0301` is an accent mark added after e. They can look like one letter while counting as two code points.
